{#
    Reqser Dynamic Custom Field Test Template

    Sibling of custom-field-test.html.twig for the dynamic-index case: the custom
    field NAME is not written in the template at all, it is read from a system-config
    value at runtime.

    Structural mirror of website 299 (GoitDefaultTheme,
    component/product/card/box-standard.html.twig): the container alias sits at template
    top level, the config binding sits inside a block, and the read is wrapped in an
    "is defined" guard. There the alias is productCustomFields, bound to
    product.translated.customFields, and the index is subTitleField, bound to
    config('GoitDefaultTheme.config.subTitle') — which resolves to the custom field
    custom_text_sub_title.

    That shape is described here in prose rather than quoted, on purpose: the scanner is
    regex-based and does not strip Twig comments, so a quoted example inside this header
    would register as a real alias and a real config binding.

    This file is never rendered — it only needs to exist on disk so the scanner can
    resolve the bound config keys and report the custom fields they point at.

    The keys used here are seeded by the Reqser test suite, not by config.xml:
      ReqserPlugin.config.reqserCustomFieldTestDynamicKey  → global + one sales channel
      ReqserPlugin.config.reqserCustomFieldTestUnsetKey    → deliberately never set
#}

{# Aliased containers at top level, exactly as the real theme declares them #}
{% set testCustomFields = category.customFields %}
{% set testTranslatedCustomFields = category.translated.customFields %}

{% block reqser_custom_field_dynamic_test %}
    {% set dynamicKeyField = config('ReqserPlugin.config.reqserCustomFieldTestDynamicKey') %}

    {# Aliased container, direct read — guarded like the real template #}
    {% if testCustomFields[dynamicKeyField] is defined %}
        {{ testCustomFields[dynamicKeyField] }}
    {% endif %}

    {# Aliased container, translated read #}
    {{ testTranslatedCustomFields[dynamicKeyField] }}

    {# Direct container, bound variable #}
    {{ category.customFields[dynamicKeyField] }}

    {# Inline config() in the index #}
    {{ category.translated.customFields[config('ReqserPlugin.config.reqserCustomFieldTestDynamicKey')] }}

    {# Literal |default harvested because the setting is never written #}
    {% set defaultedField = config('ReqserPlugin.config.reqserCustomFieldTestUnsetKey')|default('reqser_custom_field_test_dynamic_default') %}
    {{ category.customFields[defaultedField] }}

    {# Bracket-string container twin, mirroring the literal scan's fourth pass #}
    {{ category["customFields"][defaultedField] }}

    {# Negative anchor: the same bound variable indexing a map that is NOT a customFields
       container. Drop the alias-membership gate and this read starts being attributed to
       the resolved field name. The map holds no custom field name on purpose, so no literal
       pass can ever match this line either. #}
    {% set notACustomFieldsMap = { 'someOtherKey': 'noise' } %}
    {{ notACustomFieldsMap[dynamicKeyField] }}
{% endblock %}
